---
description: Prefer @emporix/api-calls methods before custom API requests
alwaysApply: true
---

# API Requests

When adding, changing, or reviewing API requests, first check whether the endpoint is already implemented in the `@emporix/api-calls` library.

- If a matching method exists in `@emporix/api-calls`, pause and ask the user whether they want to use that library method instead of a custom API call.
- If the user agrees, use the library method.
- If the user declines, continue with the custom API call approach.
- If no matching method exists in `@emporix/api-calls`, proceed with the custom API call approach.

Example prompt to the user:

`I found that this endpoint appears to be available in @emporix/api-calls. Would you like me to use that library method instead of keeping a custom API call? If not, I can continue with the custom call implementation.`
